From: openHC
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: lpc_ich: give the GPIO cell an OF compatible

lpc_ich spawns gpio_ich as an MFD cell with no .of_compatible, and
mfd_add_device() only hands a child an OF node when its cell names one. So
on an x86 board that links a device tree into the kernel (BUILTIN_DTB) the
ICH GPIO block can be described -- a node under the LPC bridge's PCI node --
but the gpiochip never sees it, and nothing in the tree can reference a
line: no gpio-leds, no gpio-keys, no gpio-line-names.

Name the cell "intel,ich-gpio". With a matching child under the LPC node,
mfd-core sets it as the child's of_node; dev_fwnode() prefers of_node, so
gpiochip_choose_fwnode() gives the gpiochip that node and phandles resolve.
Without one (every board but those that describe it), nothing changes: the
cell has no OF node, mfd_acpi_add_device() and the swnode behave as before.

The Control4 HC-800 (Atom D525 + NM10) wires its front-panel LEDs and its
ID button to ICH GPIO lines that neither its BIOS nor ACPI describes; this is
what lets its device tree, rather than a C board file, say so.

---
--- a/drivers/mfd/lpc_ich.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/lpc_ich.c
@@ -133,6 +133,7 @@
 
 static struct mfd_cell lpc_ich_gpio_cell = {
 	.name = "gpio_ich",
+	.of_compatible = "intel,ich-gpio",
 	.num_resources = ARRAY_SIZE(gpio_ich_res),
 	.resources = gpio_ich_res,
 	.ignore_resource_conflicts = true,
